{
  "schema": "english-parts/1",
  "register": "person-history",
  "description": "A person's history on their card, told as a short biography from the records the player would know of: born, school, a move, a partner, a child, work, a parent's death, the offices they won (owner, Nov 1: \"Elected legislator, it needs to be told like a story. How many times do I have to say that?\"). Each sentence of the story (person-history.story.<key>) has three forms: said of someone in the third person (the first sentence names them, the rest use their recorded pronouns), in the they form, and to the player about their own life. A run of terms in one office is one sentence. The card shows the year beside each sentence, so a sentence leaves it out. person-history.summary.<key> are the lines under the name: who they are now, and where they come from.",
  "slots": {
    "place": "A place's name from the place records.",
    "year": "The record's year.",
    "month": "The record's month and year, as people say it: January 2025.",
    "school": "The school's name as its record writes it.",
    "name": "A person's full name from their record.",
    "title": "The job's title from the job record.",
    "employer": "The employer's name from the organization record.",
    "relation": "Mother or father, from the record, in lower case.",
    "office": "The office won, in lower case: president, mayor.",
    "stage": "The school stage as its record writes it: elementary, middle or high.",
    "who": "The person the sentence is about: their full name in the story's first sentence, then their pronoun (She, He), from their record.",
    "their": "Their possessive pronoun from their record (her, his).",
    "years": "The later years they won the same office again, joined as a list: 2013 and 2015.",
    "state": "A state's name from the place records: Ohio.",
    "whom": "The person the story is about, as the object of a sentence: their full name the first time, then their pronoun (her, him)."
  },
  "maxWords": 24,
